# Depth buffer visualization — diagnostic overlay
#
# Format: PARAM_<TYPE> <name> <slot> <default> <min> <max> <description>
#         PARAM_VEC4   <name> <slot> <r> <g> <b> <a> <description>
#
# Exposed as MVP_DEPTHVIZ_<PARAM> config items while the effect is loaded.
# Tune them from the in-game console while the effect is running.

NAME Depth Buffer Visualization
DESCRIPTION Draws a grayscale depth-buffer thumbnail in the top-right corner on top of the live scene. Near surfaces are white, far surfaces are black. The display works directly on raw [0..1] depth buffer values with a tunable contrast window — no linearization, no assumed projection parameters — so it works regardless of how the projection matrix is set up. Typical gameplay depth clusters in [0.7..0.98] after perspective, so the default window [0.5..0.99] should show clear contrast out of the box.

PARAM_FLOAT size      0 0.25 0.05 0.9    Thumbnail width as a fraction of the screen
PARAM_FLOAT rawMin    1 0.5  0.0  1.0    Raw depth value mapped to WHITE (nearest — lower = closer zoom to near plane)
PARAM_FLOAT rawMax    2 0.99 0.0  1.0    Raw depth value mapped to BLACK (farthest — raise to zoom into far distance)
PARAM_FLOAT border    3 2.0  0.0  10.0   Border thickness in pixels
PARAM_VEC4  borderColor 4 1.0 1.0 0.0 1.0 Color of the rectangle outline (RGBA)
PARAM_FLOAT gamma     5 1.0  0.1  10.0   Post-gamma curve. 1 = linear; >1 brightens midtones; <1 darkens
